\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$; the standard number fields have their usual meanings. All additional conventions are stated locally.


\paragraph{Definitions and notation.}A modular or automorphic form transforms according to a specified group and weight on a parameter domain. Moduli of Calabi--Yau threefolds parametrize their geometric structures. Reduction to lower-dimensional forms may mean restriction, factorization or descent under a map of moduli spaces, and these are different operations.

\paragraph{Catalogue wording retained for traceability.}
When can modular forms on Calabi Yau 3-folds moduli spaces be reduced to lower dimensional forms?
\paragraph{Scope and source qualification.}The source leaves the modular group, domain, notion of form and reduction map unspecified. The problem is to supply and investigate a meaningful reduction theory, not assert all such objects factor. The catalogue title/status was paired with a machine-generated research attempt; that attempt is not peer-reviewed evidence of settlement. The statement covers the original source questions rather than only the title’s subcase.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Determine when modular objects on Calabi–Yau threefold moduli can reduce to lower-dimensional forms.

